{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T14:29:22.031Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"agents-v1-decision-pool-goals--2026-10-14","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"subagent_type":"coder","description":"Implement agents decision pool + board","prompt":"You are implementing a scoped feature in a NeoForge 1.21.1 Minecraft mod (Java 21, Parchment mappings, ModDevGradle) at /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/siasworkshop. Mod id `siasworkshop`, package root `com.siaws.siawsmod`.\n\n## Task\n\nImplement the \"shared decision pool + task board + comfort detectors + observation compression\" slice of the agents workstream. A previous session built the spike (entity + observation + inspector item, committed as 8bfa3b8). You are building the next layer. Do NOT commit anything. Do NOT touch `mdocs/`. Do NOT modify files outside the scope below.\n\n## Required reading (do this first, in this order)\n\n1. `mdocs/wiki/reference/agent-embodiment-observation.md` — design source of truth. Read Pillar 3 (decision pool) and Pillar 4 (goals/task board/comfort detectors) and the \"Measured budget\" section carefully.\n2. `AGENTS.md` — repo conventions (init/ holders, DeferredRegister, config gating, content/ package layout).\n3. `src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/AgentObservation.java` (396 lines — the file you will compress).\n4. `src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/AgentInspectorItem.java`, `WorkshopAgentEntity.java`, `init/SiasWorkshopEntities.java`, `SiasWorkshop.java`, `config/Config.java`, `gametest/AgentsGameTest.java`.\n5. `mdocs/wiki/setup/gametest-notes-1-21-1.md` — toolchain gotchas (single-arg `addAdditionalSaveData(CompoundTag)`; `@GameTestHolder`; template naming `<modid>:<classname>.<template>` lowercase; templates load from singular `data/<ns>/structure/`; `helper.makeMockServerPlayerInLevel()` works but is deprecated-for-removal in 21.1.256).\n6. `src/main/resources/data/siasworkshop/structure/agentsgametest.empty.nbt` — hand-generated empty GameTest structure fixture (binary). A new gametest class needs its own fixture: copy this file byte-for-byte to `src/main/resources/data/siasworkshop/structure/agentsgoalsgametest.empty.nbt` (template name is `<classname-lowercase>.<templatename-lowercase>`).\n\n## What to build\n\n### A. Shared decision pool — `content/agents/pool/`\n- `PoolEntry.java` — record/fields per design: `id` (String UUID), `tags` (List<String>), `situationSummary` (String), `plan` (List<String>), `outcome` (enum SUCCESS/FAILED + `failureReason` String), `metrics` (at minimum `durationTicks` long), `uses` int, `successes` int, `lastUsedGameTime` long, `schemaVersion` int (v1). Immutable; mutations (uses/successes/lastUsed) return copies or go through the pool class.\n- `AgentDecisionPool.java` — extends `net.minecraft.world.level.saveddata.SavedData`, per-(ServerLevel)world via `level.getDataStorage().computeIfAbsent(...)`. Persist entries to NBT (`save(CompoundTag, HolderLookup.Provider)` — verify exact 21.1.256 signature against the mapped Minecraft sources in the Gradle cache or existing repo usages), each entry tagged `schema_version=1`; unknown schema versions skipped on load (forward-compat).\n- Retrieval: `List<PoolEntry> retrieve(Collection<String> tags, int k)` — score by tag overlap; prefer `isTrusted()` (successes >= trustThreshold) then higher successes; increment `uses` + set `lastUsedGameTime` on returned entries and `setDirty()`.\n- Cap: when size exceeds maxEntries (config), evict LRU by `lastUsedGameTime` (entries never retrieved/used evict first; tie-break oldest creation).\n- `recordOutcome(...)` API used by the task board resolution hook.\n\n### B. Task board — `content/agents/tasks/`\n- `BoardTask.java` — `id`, `key` (String, e.g. `comfort:light:<playerUuid>`), `type` (enum: COMFORT_LIGHT, COMFORT_SHELTER; leave room for BUILD later), `status` (OPEN/CLAIMED/DONE/FAILED), `claimantUuid` (nullable), `leaseUntilGameTime` (long, 0 = none), `createdAtGameTime`, `resolvedAtGameTime`, `detail` (short String, e.g. deficit location), `failureReason` (nullable).\n- `TaskBoard.java` — SavedData like the pool. Operations: `raiseIfAbsent(key, type, detail)` (comfort deficit singleton: only creates when no OPEN/CLAIMED task with that key exists), `claim(taskId, claimantUuid, leaseTicks, now)` (only from OPEN, or from CLAIMED when lease expired — steals), `complete(taskId)`, `fail(taskId, reason)`, `sweepLeases(now)` (CLAIMED past lease → FAILED \"lease_expired\"), `clearIfOpen(key)` (deficit gone while OPEN → remove/mark obsolete without pool entry), `autoCompleteClaimed(key)` (deficit gone while CLAIMED → DONE with pool success record). Resolution hooks call `AgentDecisionPool.recordOutcome` with tags derived from type (e.g. `comfort`, `light`) and a one-line situation summary. All resolution paths `setDirty()`.\n\n### C. Comfort detectors — `content/agents/tasks/ComfortDetectors.java`\n- Server tick handler (register NeoForge `ServerTickEvent.Post` in `SiasWorkshop.java`; run every N ticks, N = config, default 40; only for ServerLevels; config-gated).\n- Light detector: per player, scan cube radius R (config, default 8) around player; count positions that are air, have a solid below-block, and `level.getBrightness(LightType.BLOCK, pos) < threshold` (config, default 4). Count > 0 → raise `comfort:light:<uuid>`; count == 0 → clear/auto-complete it.\n- Shelter detector: only at night (`!level.isDay()`). Deficit when no bed within radius (config, default 16) of the player OR `level.getBrightness(LightType.SKY, pos) >= 15` at the player position (exposed). Raise/clear `comfort:shelter:<uuid>` the same way.\n- Keep the scan cheap: reuse a `BlockPos.MutableBlockPos`; no allocations in the hot path beyond small counters.\n- Access pool + board per level via `level.getDataStorage()`. Wrap in a small `AgentWorldData` helper class if that keeps access tidy (your call — one clear pattern, not both).\n\n### D. Config — extend `config/Config.java` agents section\nAdd (with the existing style/pattern in that file): `agentsComfortDetectorsEnabled` (bool, default true), `agentsDetectorIntervalTicks` (int, default 40), `agentsLightScanRadius` (int, 8), `agentsLightThreshold` (int, 4), `agentsShelterRadius` (int, 16), `agentsPoolMaxEntries` (int, 256), `agentsPoolTopK` (int, 3), `agentsPoolTrustThreshold` (int, 3), `agentsObservationBudgetTokens` (int, 900). All comments per existing style.\n\n### E. SEQ-007 observation compression — `content/agents/AgentObservation.java` (+1 small new helper class, e.g. `ObservationBudget.java`)\nThe user measured a live snapshot at ~1200–1500 tokens vs the ≤900 target (see design \"Measured budget\" section). Requirements:\n- Token estimator: `tokens ≈ ceil(chars / 4)` in a small static helper; expose `estimateTokens(String)`.\n- Build sections as independent strings (SELF, PLAYERS, NEARBY BLOCKS, NEARBY ENTITIES, ENVIRONMENT, AVAILABLE ACTIONS — keep current section set/order), then enforce the budget by compressing bottom-up in salience order (ENVIRONMENT shrinks to a minimal one-liner first, then NEARBY ENTITIES drops to counts only, then NEARBY BLOCKS top-list truncated, then PLAYERS drops per-player detail down to name@distance). SELF and AVAILABLE ACTIONS always survive.\n- Compact formats throughout: inventory summary caps at 6 entries + `other×n` (already close — keep), block-count top-list cap 6 (was 8), POI lines stay one-line `name×count(+x,+y,+z)` relative coords, action names shortened: `move_to(x,z)`→`move(x,z)`, `deposit_to(chest)`→`deposit(chest)`, `withdraw_from(chest)`→`withdraw(chest)`, `light_area()`→`light()`, `claim_task(board)`→`claim()`, `build_step(blueprint)`→`build(blueprint)`, `say(player,msg)`→`say(player,msg)` (already short). Update the doc comment on `appendActions` to reflect the short names.\n- The budget value comes from config (`agentsObservationBudgetTokens`), passed into `AgentObservation.build(agent)` from its caller (`AgentInspectorItem`) — thread it as a parameter rather than reaching into Config from a static helper, so gametests can inject values.\n\n### F. SEQ-007 verbatim snapshot-to-file — `AgentInspectorItem`\nAfter sending the snapshot to chat, also write it verbatim (full uncompressed snapshot, not the budget-trimmed one if you end up with two variants — write exactly what a prompt would receive, i.e. the budget-enforced text) to `debug/siasworkshop/agent-observation-<epochMillis>.txt` under the server game directory. Verify the exact way to get a Path under the server root from the mapped sources (e.g. `MinecraftServer#getFilePath` or equivalent in 21.1.256). Create dirs with `Files.createDirectories`. Log the path to the player chat (short line, e.g. \"snapshot saved: debug/siasworkshop/agent-observation-….txt\"). Wrap IO in try/catch and report failure in chat, don't crash.\n\n### G. Gametests — `gametest/AgentsGoalsGameTest.java`\nNew `@GameTestHolder(\"siasworkshop\")` class using template `empty` (fixture file as described above). Tests (each its own @GameTest method, batch default):\n1. Pool: create pool via `helper.getLevel().getDataStorage()`, record outcomes, assert retrieve() ranks tag matches + trusted first; assert cap eviction drops least-recently-used; save/load round-trip through NBT (`pool.save(...)` → construct new via the same read function, assert equality of key fields).\n2. Board: raiseIfAbsent twice → one task; claim → second claim by other UUID fails while lease holds; `sweepLeases` past lease → FAILED \"lease_expired\"; clearIfOpen removes OPEN; autoCompleteClaimed resolves CLAIMED to DONE and writes a pool entry (assert pool size grew).\n3. Detectors: build a dark enclosed spot (set blocks to make a light-deficit, e.g. stone box with air inside, player position via `helper.makeMockServerPlayerInLevel()`), invoke the detector logic directly (expose a package-visible/test-visible method like `runOnce(ServerLevel)` so tests don't wait for ticks), assert the light task raised; then place torches / break the box, run again, assert cleared. Shelter: same pattern at night (`helper.getLevel().setDayTime(13000)` — verify the setter exists in mapped sources) with no bed → raised; add bed + cover → cleared.\n4. Budget: with a mock player in level, build the observation (refactor `AgentObservation.build` so tests can call it for an entity + injected budget, or extract a `build(agent, budgetTokens)` overload), assert `estimateTokens(snapshot) <= 900` and that SELF + AVAILABLE ACTIONS sections are present.\nKeep tests deterministic and fast: use `helper.setBlock`/`helper.getLevel()`. Note the existing `AgentsGameTest` patterns — mirror its structure.\n\n## Verification (must pass before you report)\n\n- `./gradlew build` — green.\n- `./gradlew runGameTestServer` — all tests green (existing 3 + your new ones). These Gradle runs take minutes: use `run_in_background=true` Bash with generous timeout and poll the log, do not run them in the foreground with a 60s timeout.\n- No new warnings that fail the build; match the code style of the surrounding files (javadoc on public API, no comments stating the obvious).\n\n## Report back\n\n- List of files created/modified with one-line purposes.\n- Test results: exact gametest counts (e.g. \"7/7 green\"), build status.\n- Any deviations from this brief and why; any design decisions you had to make that weren't specified.\n- Exact API surface of pool/board/detectors (method signatures) so the coordinator can review without re-reading every file."}}}
