ard with claim/lease/steal, lease sweep, singleton comfort deficit keys; light detector (air + solid floor + block light < threshold + cannot-see-sky); shelter detector at night (bed within radius AND skylight covered); observation budget enforcement bottom-up (ENVIRONMENT → ENTITIES → BLOCKS → PLAYERS; SELF+ACTIONS always kept) with ~chars/4 token estimator and 900-token default; inspector writes the snapshot verbatim to debug/siasworkshop/*.txt under the server game dir.\n\n## Review focus (in priority order)\n\n1. **Correctness bugs**: SavedData save/load round-trip fidelity (UUID/enum/long/int list handling, `setDirty` coverage), lease steal logic (boundary: leaseUntil == now — should be expired), claim race semantics, LRU eviction ordering (never-used first, then lastUsed, then oldest), detector scan correctness (mutable BlockPos reuse, canSeeSky/light-level API usage on 21.1.256, per-player loops), NBT null-safety on read (missing keys, malformed tags).\n2. **Concurrency/thread-safety**: everything must run on the server thread; check the tick handler and SavedData access patterns.\n3. **Performance**: detector scan cost per interval (cube radius 8 = ~4.6k positions/player — acceptable?); observation build allocations; pool eviction on every recordOutcome.\n4. **Design fidelity**: does anything contradict the design brief (e.g. pool entries containing non-action-space text, comfort tasks not being singletons, budget enforcement dropping SELF or ACTIONS)?\n5. **Test quality**: do the 8 new gametests actually assert the behaviors above, or are any tautological? Any test that could pass with the implementation broken?\n6. **Repo conventions**: init/ holder discipline, config gating, lang keys prefixed `siasworkshop.`, no stray comments.\n\n## Report format\n\nFor each finding: severity (blocking / should-fix / nit), file:line, one-paragraph explanation, suggested fix. End with an overall verdict: APPROVE / APPROVE-WITH-NITS / REQUEST-CHANGES. Be specific and skeptical — if you find nothing blocking, say so explicitly after checking the focus areas above.","subagent_type":"plan"}}}
