{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T19:28:52.409Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"agents-v1-llm-build-knowledge--2026-10-14","step":"UNDERSTAND","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"## Plan\nDesign sources: `reference/local-llm-feasibility` (client principles: constrained JSON, template fallback, off-thread + server.execute hop-back, offline-first, enabled=false default) and `reference/agent-embodiment-observation` pillar 4 + \"Build knowledge\" table (own parsers — never copy WorldEdit/Litematica; retrieve-and-inject; grief guardrails). Carry-overs from SEQ-008 folded in: task-execution loop, currentTask() wiring, pool recordSuccess citations. Endpoint verified live 2026-10-14: LM Studio at `http://localhost:1234/v1`, model id `prism-ml/bonsai-27b` present.\n\n- [ ] LLM client `content/llm/` — OpenAI-compatible chat completions (java.net.http, no new deps), config: llmEnabled(false), llmEndpoint(default `http://localhost:1234/v1`), llmModel(default `prism-ml/bonsai-27b`), llmTimeoutSeconds(30), llmMaxTokens(64), llmTemperature(0.3); dedicated single-thread executor, hop back via `server.execute`, one request in flight per agent, defensive JSON parse, silent template fallback on any failure (offline-first: no player-visible errors)\n- [ ] Blueprint model `content/agents/build/` — Blueprint{name, size, List<Placement(block, relPos)>} + own parsers: Sponge .schem v2/v3 and vanilla structure .nbt (our own format interpretation on top of vanilla NBT IO — no copied parser code); import folder `config/siasworkshop/blueprints/` scanned at server start\n- [ ] Build queue — player-enqueueable blueprint tasks (server command `/siasworkshop build <name> <x> <y> <z>` v1; foundation GUI later), BoardTask.Type.BUILD already reserved; materials sourced from agent inventory after withdraw-from-nearby-chest step; missing materials → fail(reason) (legit pool anti-pattern)\n- [ ] Build-card datapack JSON loader — `data/<ns>/siasworkshop_build_cards/*.json` {name, style_tags[], size, materials_list{}, palette[], step_summary, source_note}; loaded on datapack reload; tag-match retrieval for prompt injection (retrieve-and-inject, never browse)\n- [ ] Agent decision/execution loop — server tick, config cadence (agentsDecisionIntervalSeconds, default 30): idle agent → observation (budget config) → pool.retrieve(topK) → LLM picks one JSON action from the validated action space (parse+validate, else fallback) or template fallback: claim highest-priority OPEN task (comfort first), execute fixed plans (light: path to deficit, place torches from inventory, lease renewals; shelter/build per queue); resolution via claimant-verified board API + recordSuccess/recordOutcome citations; currentTask() wired to claimed task; adds TaskBoard.release(taskId, claimant) for clean unclaim (no pool write)\n- [ ] Grief guardrails — break/place only within village-bounds radius of an approved anchor (task/deficit/blueprint anchor); block whitelist per task type (torch for light, blueprint palette for builds); every executed action logged (debug log + chronicle hook point)\n- [ ] Gametests — parsers round-trip (fixture .schem v3 + .nbt written in-test), build-card codec parse, LLM client against a loopback stub HTTP server (success/timeout/malformed → fallback paths), light-task end-to-end (claim → place torch → detector clears → DONE → pool success), build task places blueprint blocks from mocked inventory\n- [ ] `./gradlew build` + `runGameTestServer` green, review, `mdocs validate`\n\n## Progress Log\n- [2026-10-14T05:54:12.293Z] Created initiative via mdocs command\n- [2026-10-14T15:45:00.000Z] Resumed; LM Studio endpoint verified live (GET /v1/models → `prism-ml/bonsai-27b` et al.). Plan expanded with SEQ-008 carry-overs (execution loop, currentTask wiring) and guardrails.","oldString":"## Plan\n- [ ] LLM client + Config.java keys + fallback\n- [ ] Blueprint model + template build queue\n- [ ] Own .schem/.nbt parser + import folder\n- [ ] Build-card datapack JSON loader\n- [ ] Gametests, review, validate\n\n## Progress Log\n- [2026-10-14T05:54:12.293Z] Created initiative via mdocs command","path":"mdocs/initiatives/agents-v1-llm-build-knowledge-2026-10-14--2026-10-14.md"}}}
