{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T06:33:18.433Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"agents-v1-llm-build-knowledge--2026-10-14","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Apply review fixes to LLM slice","prompt":"Review of the LLM slice came back REQUEST-CHANGES. Apply the fixes below to the uncommitted diff at /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/siasworkshop (NeoForge 1.21.1, Java 21). Do NOT commit; do NOT touch mdocs/. Then run `./gradlew build` and `./gradlew runGameTestServer` ONCE (background, long timeout). If anything is still red after your fixes, report exactly what's red — do NOT start a debugging spiral; the coordinator will take over.\n\n## Blocking\n\n1. **Air kept as placement** — `SchemParser.java` (~line 87): skip `minecraft:air`/`cave_air`/`void_air` entries when building Placements (document in the class javadoc: schematics store air explicitly; agents must not \"place air\"). Add a parser round-trip test in AgentsLlmGameTest with air entries in BlockData (assert they're skipped, solids survive).\n2. **Hostile input escapes BlueprintParseException** — `SchemParser.java` + `StructureNbtParser.java`:\n   - Wrap dimension math in try/catch: `Math.multiplyExact` overflow → BlueprintParseException(\"unreasonable dimensions\").\n   - Volume cap: width*height*length > 512_000 → BlueprintParseException (blueprints are small structures).\n   - v2 palette: reject index >= palette size with BlueprintParseException instead of growing the list.\n   - Replace `NbtAccounter.unlimitedHeap()` with a bounded accounter (e.g. `NbtAccounter.create(64 * 1024 * 1024)`) in both parsers; wrap any IOException/RuntimeException from NbtIo.readCompressed in BlueprintParseException so `BlueprintLibrary.reload` never propagates.\n\n## Should-fix\n\n3. **Bad llm.endpoint throws on server thread + permanently stalls the agent** — `LlmClient.requestRaw` (~line 92): catch RuntimeException around URI/request construction and return the failed LlmResult (e.g. reason \"bad_endpoint\"). In `AgentDecisionLoop.decide`, ensure `inFlightRequests` is cleared even if the request call itself throws (guard with try/finally or move the add after validation — pick one clean approach).\n4. **Stale `now` in LLM callback** — `AgentDecisionLoop.decide`: the completion callback captures `now` from decision time; a slow reply (>leaseTicks=200) claims a task born-expired → swept FAILED; build tasks never re-raise. Capture `level.getGameTime()` fresh inside the callback and use it for the claim/applyDecisionAction path.\n5. **Static maps leak** — AgentDecisionLoop's lastPositions/stuckCycles/pendingCitations/inFlightRequests: add a `ServerStoppingEvent` handler (register in SiasWorkshop.java next to the existing listeners) clearing all four. That covers world restart in the same JVM; skip per-entity pruning.\n6. **Blueprint names with spaces break the detail round-trip** — normalize at load in `BlueprintLibrary.reload`: replace spaces with `_` in blueprint names (both lookup key and stored name), WARN once per renamed file.\n7. **resolveCitations credits stale retrievals after FAILED** — in `AgentDecisionLoop.resolveCitations`: also clear pendingCitations when a task this agent claimed resolves FAILED (mirroring the DONE branch).\n8. **guardRadius < lightScanRadius churn** — Config.java: extend the guardRadius comment to document the invariant (guardRadius should be >= lightScanRadius for light tasks to be executable); no code change.\n9. **Gametest isolation is timing luck** — build.gradle seeded TOML: also pin `agents.decisionIntervalSeconds = 600` in the seeded `siasworkshop-server.toml` (same doFirst block), with the comment noting the global decision pass must not fire mid-test.\n\n## Nits (apply)\n\n10. `AgentDecisionLoop`: swap consumeItem/setBlock order in both executors (setBlock first, consume only on success); fix fully-qualified inline names to imports (SiasWorkshop.LOGGER, Blocks.TORCH, java.util.Set, JsonArray in LlmClient); fix the stale AGENTS_DECISION_INTERVAL_SECONDS comment (decisions only; execution is per-tick).\n11. `BuildCards`: drop the double parse (pass the JsonElement through); reject zero/negative sizes in parseSize.\n\n## Skip (documented, not code)\n\n- BuildCommand lang keys (v1 acceptable), StructureNbtParser pos-bounds check, palettes-plural test, LlmActions shape matrix tests, bedrock/spawner material note — leave as-is.\n\n## Report\n\nFix confirmations with file:line, the new test name(s), and the exact build + gametest results from your runs (test counts). List any fix you could not apply.","resume":"agent-0"}}}
