{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:05:35.346Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"`SEQ-021 | 2026-10-16 | coordinator | RESOLVED | S2 done in the sidecar harness: the six-step building pattern walk runs end-to-end — think_through_request → analyze_terrain → design → select_materials → create_blueprint → apply_blueprint → observe_task polling until DONE. D5 situational card gating enforced session-side (a tool works only after the card offering it opened; replay asserts an early apply_blueprint gets gate-rejected and the model recovers); prompt + native modes; mock simulates mod-side machinery (site ranking, cards, material bills, blueprint store, build advancing one tick per poll). RESULTS: walk replay 3/3 (S0 regression still 20/20); cloud deepseek native 2/2 converged on the exact reference chain (20.8s/779 tok, 26.2s/1101 tok — one run self-recovered from 3 exec rejects); local bonsai prompt-mode 1/1 converged on the full chain (127s, 1496 tok, 2 rejects recovered) — a 27B reasoning model completes a 6-step MCP workflow in prompt-constrained-JSON mode. Spike bugs found+fixed: (1) session allowed-set UPDATE filtered the old set instead of UNIONING card children (the gate could never open — caught by replay); (2) POS_REF was a bare string not a {\"$ref\":...} dict (validator crash on first pos arg); (3) pattern vs effect result shape inconsistency ({result,children} cards vs plain top-level) broke convergence polling. Also: WalkResult gained reject_details for step-level forensics (the corpus phase will need it). User will live-test the sidecar now that S2 lands. Next: S1 (in-mod MCP client behind agents.mcp.enabled + gametest) or scenario corpus (Q4) — user picks.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED","oldString":"`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:05:35.351Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"`SEQ-021 | 2026-10-16 | coordinator | RESOLVED | S2 done in the sidecar harness: the six-step building pattern walk runs end-to-end — think_through_request → analyze_terrain → design → select_materials → create_blueprint → apply_blueprint → observe_task polling until DONE. D5 situational card gating enforced session-side (a tool works only after the card offering it opened; replay asserts an early apply_blueprint gets gate-rejected and the model recovers); prompt + native modes; mock simulates mod-side machinery (site ranking, cards, material bills, blueprint store, build advancing one tick per poll). RESULTS: walk replay 3/3 (S0 regression still 20/20); cloud deepseek native 2/2 converged on the exact reference chain (20.8s/779 tok, 26.2s/1101 tok — one run self-recovered from 3 exec rejects); local bonsai prompt-mode 1/1 converged on the full chain (127s, 1496 tok, 2 rejects recovered) — a 27B reasoning model completes a 6-step MCP workflow in prompt-constrained-JSON mode. Spike bugs found+fixed: (1) session allowed-set UPDATE filtered the old set instead of UNIONING card children (the gate could never open — caught by replay); (2) POS_REF was a bare string not a {\"$ref\":...} dict (validator crash on first pos arg); (3) pattern vs effect result shape inconsistency ({result,children} cards vs plain top-level) broke convergence polling. Also: WalkResult gained reject_details for step-level forensics (the corpus phase will need it). User will live-test the sidecar now that S2 lands. Next: S1 (in-mod MCP client behind agents.mcp.enabled + gametest) or scenario corpus (Q4) — user picks.`\n\n`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED","oldString":"`SEQ-011 | 2026-10-15 | coordinator | RESOLVED | Live smoke tests 1-3 ALL PASSED","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/agent-shared-ledger.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:05:51.642Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"## S2 walk results (2026-10-16)\n\nThe six-step building walk runs end-to-end in the sidecar harness (ledger SEQ-021):\nD5 card gating session-side, prompt + native modes, convergence by `observe_task`\npolling (mock advances the build one tick per poll).\n\n- **Cloud deepseek native: 2/2 converged on the exact reference chain** (20.8s/779 tok;\n  26.2s/1101 tok). One run self-recovered from 3 exec rejects — reject-and-retry is a\n  viable correction loop, not just a failure mode.\n- **Local bonsai-27b prompt-mode: 1/1 converged** on the full chain (127s, 1496 tok, 2\n  rejects recovered) — a 27B reasoning model completes a 6-step MCP workflow in\n  prompt-constrained-JSON mode; the budget-containment effect from S0 holds across a\n  longer horizon.\n- Walk replay: 3/3 asserted walks (happy path ×2 modes, gate-reject recovery); S0\n  regression stays 20/20.\n- `WalkResult.reject_details` now records step-level rejects for the scenario corpus\n  (Q4).\n\n## Spike plan (next, per initiative)","oldString":"## Spike plan (next, per initiative)","path":"mdocs/wiki/reference/mcp-pattern-tree-design.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:05:51.654Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"## S2 walk results (2026-10-16)\n\nThe six-step building walk runs end-to-end in the sidecar harness (ledger SEQ-021):\nD5 card gating session-side, prompt + native modes, convergence by `observe_task`\npolling (mock advances the build one tick per poll).\n\n- **Cloud deepseek native: 2/2 converged on the exact reference chain** (20.8s/779 tok;\n  26.2s/1101 tok). One run self-recovered from 3 exec rejects — reject-and-retry is a\n  viable correction loop, not just a failure mode.\n- **Local bonsai-27b prompt-mode: 1/1 converged** on the full chain (127s, 1496 tok, 2\n  rejects recovered) — a 27B reasoning model completes a 6-step MCP workflow in\n  prompt-constrained-JSON mode; the budget-containment effect from S0 holds across a\n  longer horizon.\n- Walk replay: 3/3 asserted walks (happy path ×2 modes, gate-reject recovery); S0\n  regression stays 20/20.\n- `WalkResult.reject_details` now records step-level rejects for the scenario corpus\n  (Q4).\n\n## Spike plan (next, per initiative)","oldString":"## Spike plan (next, per initiative)","path":"mdocs/wiki/reference/mcp-pattern-tree-design.md"}}}
