{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T06:12:01.351Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"path":"src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/AgentDecisionLoop.java","oldString":" * The agent decision/execution loop (design pillars 3+4): idle agents pick ONE action — an\n * LLM-chosen action when {@code llm.enabled}, otherwise the built-in template fallback — then\n * claim a task-board task and execute it with vanilla-style steering. Java executes; the LLM\n * (if any) only decides, and only inside the validated {@link LlmActions} contract.","newString":" * The agent decision/execution loop (design pillars 3+4): idle agents pick ONE action —\n * through the MCP sidecar when {@code agents.mcp.enabled} (takes precedence, needs nothing\n * from llm.*), else an LLM-chosen action when {@code llm.enabled}, else the built-in template\n * fallback — then claim a task-board task and execute it with vanilla-style steering. Java\n * executes; the model (if any) only decides, through either the MCP tool surface or the\n * validated {@link LlmActions} contract."}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T06:12:01.357Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mcp-model-behavior-research--2026-10-15","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"path":"src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/content/agents/AgentDecisionLoop.java","oldString":" * The agent decision/execution loop (design pillars 3+4): idle agents pick ONE action — an\n * LLM-chosen action when {@code llm.enabled}, otherwise the built-in template fallback — then\n * claim a task-board task and execute it with vanilla-style steering. Java executes; the LLM\n * (if any) only decides, and only inside the validated {@link LlmActions} contract.","newString":" * The agent decision/execution loop (design pillars 3+4): idle agents pick ONE action —\n * through the MCP sidecar when {@code agents.mcp.enabled} (takes precedence, needs nothing\n * from llm.*), else an LLM-chosen action when {@code llm.enabled}, else the built-in template\n * fallback — then claim a task-board task and execute it with vanilla-style steering. Java\n * executes; the model (if any) only decides, through either the MCP tool surface or the\n * validated {@link LlmActions} contract."}}}
